## Sales Performance

![Sales Performance](Sales_Performance.png)

This dashboard analyses regional sales performance using the retail dataset transformed from SQL and modelled in Power BI.

The objective of this analysis was to understand how sales performance varies across countries, identify high-performing markets, and explore the relationship between units sold and revenue generation.

Key metrics displayed include:

• **Total Orders** – overall number of orders processed  
• **Average Revenue per Country** – average revenue contribution by market  
• **Average Order Value by Country** – comparison of revenue generated per order across different countries  

The **Average Order Value by Country** chart highlights differences in purchasing behaviour across markets, showing which regions generate higher value transactions.

The **Revenue vs Units Sold scatter plot** illustrates the relationship between product demand and total revenue by country. This helps identify:

- high-volume markets generating strong revenue  
- markets with higher-value orders but lower sales volume  
- emerging markets with growing demand  

The analysis shows that sales are heavily concentrated in the **United Kingdom**, which significantly outperforms other markets in both revenue and units sold. Other European markets contribute steady sales volumes but remain smaller in comparison.

This dashboard demonstrates how geographic sales analysis can support business decisions such as market expansion, regional marketing strategies, and sales performance monitoring.
